# St. Lawrence Seaway and USCG PAWSS AIS binary messages (DAC 316 and 366): FI 1 meteorological and
# hydrological reports (weather, wind, water level, current, salinity and temperature, water flow), FI 2 lock
# scheduling (lockage order, estimated lock times), FI 32 version. The input is the armored payload of a type 6
# or type 8 message. Written by tools/gen/ais-regional-pack.py; do not edit by hand.
format        ais-binary-regional
version       0.1.0
distribution  public
source        "St. Lawrence Seaway AIS Data Messaging Formats and Specifications, Harmonized with U.S. Coast Guard PAWSS AIS Messages, Revision 4.1, April 9, 2010 (U.S. DOT Volpe Center for the SLSDC and SLSMC), https://greatlakes-seaway.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/05/Seaway-AIS-message-specifications-R41.pdf (sha256 79da3b8f29acf7543ff440903769a702c98bd7dc4dba438720c75150262b917d), no licence stated; layout restated"
